    <string name="route_priority_auto_explanation">Auto: Wi-Fi tries Direct, VPS Relay, Worker, then Cloudflare CDN; mobile data tries VPS Relay, Worker/Cloudflare, then Direct. An unconfigured Relay is simply skipped. Failures and cooldowns temporarily move unhealthy routes down.</string>
    <string name="route_priority_direct_explanation">Direct first, followed by VPS Relay, Cloudflare Worker, and Cloudflare CDN. The app automatically advances after a route failure.</string>
    <string name="route_priority_cloudflare_explanation">Custom Cloudflare first, followed by Worker and the public Cloudflare pool, then VPS Relay and Direct. Failures, cooldowns, and verified quality still affect selection.</string>
    <string name="route_priority_relay_explanation">VPS Relay first, followed by Cloudflare and Direct. If Relay stops responding, Telegram is automatically moved to the next working route.</string>
